    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0017",
      "sequence": 29,
      "meaning": "I salute Videha, king Janaka, with his household; he bore deep love for Rāma’s feet, concealed amid yoga and enjoyment until it appeared when he saw Rāma. First I salute Bharata’s feet: his discipline and vows cannot be described; his mind, a greedy bee, never leaves the lotus of Rāma’s feet. I bow to Lakṣmaṇa’s lotus feet, cool, beautiful and joy-giving to devotees. His fame became the staff of Raghupati’s spotless banner. He is thousand-headed Śeṣa, cause of the world, descended to earth to remove fear; may compassionate, virtuous Sumitrā’s son always favour me. I bow at the lotus feet of Śatrughna, heroic, gentle and devoted to Bharata. I petition mighty Hanumān, whose glory Rāma himself proclaimed. I salute the Wind’s son, a fire to the forest of wickedness and a treasury of knowledge; in the mansion of his heart dwells Rāma bearing arrow and bow.",
