    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0018",
      "sequence": 30,
      "meaning": "I bow at the beautiful feet of Sugrīva the monkey king, Jāmbavān the bear, Vibhīṣaṇa the rākṣasa king, Aṅgada and all the monkey host: in lowly bodies they attained Rāma. I bow at the lotus feet of every worshipper of Raghupati—birds, animals, gods, humans and asuras alike—who serve Rāma without selfish desire. I salute Śuka, Sanaka and the other devoted sages, and Nārada, those excellent sages skilled in spiritual knowledge. Placing my head on the ground, I bow to all; knowing me as their servant, may the great sages show grace. Jānakī, Janaka’s daughter and mother of the world, is exceedingly dear to the treasury of compassion. I propitiate her two lotus feet, by whose grace I may gain a pure understanding. Then in mind, speech and action I bow to the all-worthy lotus feet of Raghunāyaka, lotus-eyed, bearing bow and arrow, destroyer of devotees’ distress and giver of joy. Speech and meaning are said to be distinct yet inseparable, like water and its wave; I bow to Sītā and Rāma’s feet, supremely dear to the afflicted.",
