    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0020",
      "sequence": 32,
      "meaning": "The two syllables are sweet and enchanting, the eyes of the alphabet and the life of devotees. Remembering them is easy and joy-giving for everyone: they yield benefit in this world and sustain the next. Speaking, hearing and remembering them is supremely good; they are as dear to Tulsī as Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa. When described, the syllables’ distinct affection becomes apparent, yet they are naturally joined like Brahman and the individual soul. They are good brothers like Nara and Nārāyaṇa, protectors of the world and especially of devotees. They adorn the ears of the fair lady Devotion and are the stainless moon and sun for the world’s welfare. They are respectively flavour and contentment in the nectar of liberation, and like the Tortoise and Śeṣa in supporting the earth. They are bees in the lovely lotus of the devotee’s mind, and Hari and Haladhara with the tongue as their mother Yaśodā. One is an umbrella and one a crown jewel over all letters; thus, says Tulsī, both letters of Raghubara’s name reign.",
