    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0021",
      "sequence": 33,
      "meaning": "Understood rightly, the name and the named are alike, with mutual love as lord and follower. Name and form are the Lord’s two designations, indescribable and beginningless, mastered through right understanding. To call one greater or smaller is an offence; hearing the distinction in their qualities, saints will understand. Form is seen as dependent on name, for without name no knowledge of form is possible. Even when a particular form is held in one’s palm, without knowing its name it cannot be recognized. Conversely, remember a name without seeing the form and the form comes into the heart with special affection. The relation of name and form is an ineffable story—joyful to understand but impossible to describe. Between the attributeless and attributed Lord, the name is a fine witness, awakening knowledge of both like a skilled interpreter. Place the jewel-lamp of Rāma’s name at the doorway-threshold of the tongue, says Tulsī, if you desire light within and without.",
