    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0022",
      "sequence": 34,
      "meaning": "Repeating the name upon their tongues, yogīs remain awake, detached from the creation fashioned by Brahmā, and experience the incomparable bliss of Brahman—indescribable, flawless, nameless and formless. Those who seek to know the hidden course also learn it by repeating the name upon the tongue. Practitioners repeat the name with absorbed attention and, gaining powers such as aṇimā, become accomplished. People in great distress repeat the name; severe calamities vanish and they become happy. The world has four kinds of Rāma devotees, all four meritorious, sinless and noble. The name supports all four discerning types, though the knower is especially dear to the Lord. The name’s power is known through the four ages and four Vedas, but in Kali especially there is no other means. Those free of every desire and absorbed in the nectar of Rāma devotion have made their minds fish in the lake of the nectar of supreme love for the name.",
