    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0023",
      "sequence": 35,
      "meaning": "The attributeless and attributed are two forms of Brahman, indescribable, unfathomable, beginningless and unequalled. In my judgment the name is greater than both, for by its own power it has brought both under its sway. Good people should not take this as a servant’s presumptuous assertion: I tell the conviction, love and inclination of my mind. Discern the two Brahmans like fire: one latent within wood and the other visibly blazing. Both are inaccessible, yet both become accessible through the name; therefore I have said the name is greater than Brahman and than Rāma. The one all-pervading, imperishable Brahman is existence and consciousness, a compact mass and treasury of bliss. Though such an unchanging Lord is present in the heart, every creature in the world remains poor and sorrowful. Through exposition of the name and disciplined engagement with the name, that very Lord becomes manifest, as a jewel becomes known through its assessed value. In this way the name exceeds the attributeless, and its power is boundless. According to my own reflection, I say the name is greater even than Rāma.",
