    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0024",
      "sequence": 36,
      "meaning": "For devotees’ welfare Rāma assumed a human body, endured hardships and made saints happy. By lovingly repeating the name without exertion, devotees themselves become abodes of joy and auspiciousness. Rāma delivered one ascetic’s wife, Ahalyā; the name has corrected the corrupt understanding of millions of wicked people. For the sage’s welfare Rāma destroyed Tāṭakā, daughter of Suketu, together with her son and army; the name destroys a servant’s bad hopes together with faults and sorrows, as the sun destroys night. Rāma himself broke Śiva’s bow, while the name’s glory breaks the fear of worldly existence. The Lord made the Daṇḍaka forest beautiful; the name has purified the limitless minds of people. Raghunandana destroyed hosts of night-roamers, while the name uproots every stain of Kali. Raghunātha granted a good destiny to Śabarī, Jaṭāyu and faithful servants; the name has delivered countless wicked people, as the Veda’s celebrated account of its virtues attests.",
