    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0025",
      "sequence": 37,
      "meaning": "Everyone knows that Rāma took Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa under refuge, but the name has favoured countless poor people; its excellent renown shines in the world and the Veda. Rāma gathered an army of bears and monkeys and undertook no small labour to build the bridge. At the taking of the name, the ocean of becoming dries up—reflect on this within your mind, good people. Rāma slew Rāvaṇa with his clan in battle and returned with Sītā to his own city; king Rāma ruled Ayodhyā while gods and sages sang his virtues in excellent speech. A servant who lovingly remembers the name effortlessly conquers the mighty army of delusion, moves immersed in affection and personal joy, and by the name’s grace knows no anxiety even in dreams. The name is greater than Brahman and Rāma, granting boons even to the boon-givers. From the hundred crore verses of Rāma’s story, Śiva knowingly took it into his heart.",
